# ---------- check-motion-areas (wave-67) ----------
# Trigger: any change in the 22 wave-67-tracked component trees (same set as
# wave-65's shadow ratchet — pages + dashboard + landing + recruiter + 18
# v24/v25-cleaned sibling trees), or the script itself.
# Mechanic: ratchets v22 §10 motion-fast budget violations per area at the
# measured floor at lock time (HEAD 85ec4826). Counts arbitrary
# `duration-[Xms]` where X > 200 + Tailwind defaults
# `duration-(300|500|700|1000|1500|2000)`. The budget is 120ms (--motion-fast
# token); --motion-base ceiling is 200ms. `duration-75/100/150/200` are inside
# the budget and not counted. Default `transition-colors` (no duration class)
# is not counted either — Tailwind's 150ms default is inside the budget.
# Why this matters: AgentLink/Cursor/Linear all sit at 120-180ms because
# that's the perceptual ceiling for "instant response". Sam's site has dozens
# of `transition-all duration-300` reaches because that's Tailwind's first
# suggested ladder beyond `duration-100`. No gate watched motion until now.
# Same persistence-mandate drift class as the bg-gradient + shadow ratchets.
# Cost when fired: ~120ms (linear in tracked-area file count).
# Opt-in marker per line for legitimate progress-bar fills, animation timing,
# or brand-decor stroke draws: `motion-budget-allow:<reason>` same-line or
# line directly above.
if match '^(src/(pages|components/(dashboard|landing|recruiter|admin|agent|awards|callcenter|celebrations|command|contentwheel|course|crm|deals|finances|layout|next-step|pipeline|plaque|profile|system-health|ui))/.+\.(tsx?|jsx?)$|scripts/check-motion-areas\.mjs$)'; then
