# technique regardless of which bg feeds it (rainbow `from-X via-Y to-Z`,
# solid `bg-white`, brand `bg-primary`). Without text-transparent the
# bg-clip-text is a no-op, and without bg-clip-text the text-transparent makes
# text invisible — so the pair IS the banned technique.
# Why this matters: wave-62 (commit a0d8fcdc) killed the rainbow titles in
# AgentPortal but the technique still ships in 5 src/pages locations as the
# wave-62 codemod-cleaned degraded solid-bg-clip form (bg-white dark:bg-slate-900
# bg-clip-text text-transparent). AgentLink/Linear/Cursor/Vercel ship solid
# headlines on a single brand color, no text-clip technique anywhere. Without
# this gate, the next new headline that drifts back to rainbow gradients has
# nothing watching. Cost when fired: ~120ms (linear in tracked-area files).
# Opt-in marker per line for legitimate hero/CTA/banner narration:
# `rainbow-title-allow:<reason>` same-line or line directly above.
if match '^(src/(pages|components/(dashboard|landing|recruiter|admin|agent|awards|callcenter|celebrations|command|contentwheel|course|crm|deals|finances|layout|next-step|pipeline|plaque|profile|system-health|ui))/.+\.(tsx?|jsx?)$|scripts/check-rainbow-title-areas\.mjs$)'; then
  echo "[pre-commit] Tracked component-tree change — running check:rainbow-title-areas…"
  node scripts/check-rainbow-title-areas.mjs
fi

